// Prisma schema. Owned by the architect; no other agent edits this file
// (`ai-rules/policy_architecture.md` -> Schema and migrations).
//
// There are no models yet, and that is deliberate. `specs/001-hello-world.md`
// renders without touching the database, and the domain entities described in
// `specs/functional/` - clients, missions, time entries, invoices - arrive
// with feature v01-001 onward, each through the normal workflow with its own
// spec. A speculative table is worse than no table: it becomes a migration
// someone has to undo.
//
// There is also no `prisma/migrations/` directory yet, for the same reason.
// `prisma migrate dev` creates nothing from a model-less schema, and
// `prisma migrate deploy` exits 0 without one while still creating the SQLite
// file - so `docker/entrypoint.sh` and the health check both work today. The
// first migration, and `migration_lock.toml` with it, arrive with the first
// real model (AD-020).

// The v7 generator. It emits TypeScript source into the directory below
// rather than patching `node_modules/.prisma`, which is why the output path
// is explicit and why `src/generated/` is git-ignored: this is build output
// that happens to live in the source tree, recreated by `prisma generate`.
//
// `src/generated/` rather than a folder under `src/lib/`, because everything
// else in `src/` is hand-written and the boundary has to be obvious to both a
// reader and an ignore file. Only `src/lib/db.ts` and the feature repositories
// may import from it (AD-004).
generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client"
  output   = "../src/generated/prisma"
}

// No `url` here: Prisma 7 removed it from the schema. The connection string
// lives in `prisma.config.ts` at the repository root for Migrate, and reaches
// the client at runtime through the driver adapter (AD-020). DATABASE_URL
// itself is still the single source of truth, validated in `src/lib/config.ts`
// (AD-013, AD-014).
datasource db {
  provider = "sqlite"
}
